    "Accept factor-72 separation and strict threshold on the original stated domain.",
    "Padded degree-two resultant removes the nonzero-constant restriction; degree-deficient inputs require projective factors.",
    "Pairwise-zero primitive quadratic families have a common linear factor, a single irreducible quadratic, or a three-edge triangle.",
    "Linear factors satisfy H(u)H(v) <= sqrt(3) H; all reducible height-H quadratics number O(H^2 log(2H)).",
    "A common-factor family has R=V+c 1^T; even kernels agree after one parity condition, with at most one odd coset.",
    "No d-rank bound for the broader reducible selector; primitive irreducible candidates alone number at most d per f.",
    "Exact global-resultant selector with eta=2/5 is a priced next counting question, not an established useful tail or factoring algorithm."
